WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.020
They look good.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.480
I was interested in this shop.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.600
It's quite packed.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.320
Oh, there's a variety of pastries too. They look good.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.070
Three months have passed since the shop opened.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.070
This Mont Blanc is quite famous, isn't it?

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.190
Thanks to our customers,

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.550
this is made using Japanese chestnuts,

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.330
so rich in flavor that you can almost taste autumn.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.100
The business is in the best possible condition.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.240
As a result of TV and magazine interviews,

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.360
our shop has become a bit famous.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.010
Oh my! This tastes great!

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.420
Chi-chan, this cake is good!

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.380
Really? Then I want one too!

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:43.230
Indeed it is!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.050
I'm really impressed.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:46.770
Can I have another?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:47.230
Of course.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.990
Our regular customers came to rely on us,

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.860
and sensei was baking to the best of his ability as well.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.940
Everything was going well.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.010
But...

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:22.480
The winter wind brought an awful man.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:48.040
Aside from him being a foreigner, those red roses...

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.380
Excuse me.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.450
Isn't this Monsieur Yuusuke Ono's pâtisserie?

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.410
No. This is my shop.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.340
I've never heard such ironic French, just like an announcer.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.840
So this shop must be trash.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.010
What!

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.500
You must be one of the men Ono picked up.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.710
If you have business with Ono, come again after we close!

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.440
By the way, he speaks Japanese.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.330
Jean Baptiste!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.370
If it isn't you, Jean Baptiste!

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.580
Why are you in Japan?

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.580
To offer my love to you once again, like this...

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:03.920
mon amour.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.020
This is Jean Baptiste Hevens.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.600
Probably one of the most famous pâtissiers in France.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.940
And he's my teacher.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.670
M-My sensei's teacher?

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.290
So he's like my super-sensei.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.360
I won't even mind if you pursue me!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.030
Umm... He wouldn't consider that a joke.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.080
Yuusuke.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.580
Can I have one each of this shop's Choux à la crème and financier?

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.110
Oui, monsieur.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.400
Not bad.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.450
I'm glad...

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.430
What a nice smile.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.870
My Adonis who never changes.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:09.240
If you two bring your faces any closer, I'll kill you.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.280
What a jealous man.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.170
If you're like that, Yuusuke will dump you soon.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.890
First of all, we're not seeing each other!

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.980
I don't like this man.
I don't like this man.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.930
Is that mutual hatred? Is that mutual hatred?

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.050
I assume there's going to be trouble.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.650
Red roses attract attention.

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:41.320
That embarrassed me a bit.

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:48.950
Didn't I say

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.920
that I came to Japan to offer you my love?

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.370
Let me in.

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.110
Liar.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.200
I'm an afterthought to your work, aren't I?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.460
I know you have a job at the Hotel Il Mare.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.720
You're more important than work.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.540
Come in.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:11.930
Someone might see us.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.280
I warn you, becoming a pâtissier requires many sacrifices,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.150
not counting the sleepless nights!

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:24.820
Furthermore, I'm somewhat impatient...

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.920
and that can make me quite violent!

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.260
No problem. I'll do whatever you want. Please give me a job...

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.230
It doesn't matter what you do! How clumsy!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:40.930
Yes, sir...

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:46.310
No! I told you that's not the way!

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:47.270
Yes, sir...

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.510
It's completely ruined! You must always watch the baking!

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.530
Start again!!

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.350
Oui, monsieur...

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.310
Yuusuke... are you all right?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.500
Yes, sir!

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.090
You've worked hard.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:12.340
Forgive me, Yuusuke. What have I done to these pretty hands?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.110
Yuusuke, mon amour.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.230
Our life together was like a French movie.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:35.190
In the first fifteen minutes, we met and went to bed.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:42.330
And in the remaining hour and 45 minutes, we fought and broke up.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.170
Yuusuke...

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.960
So, as I thought, he's your ex-boyfriend.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:56.450
Yeah. But he's more like a great teacher to me.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.290
I learned everything about confectionery from him.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.750
So he must be a great person.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.860
Yeah.

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:07.090
But how did you two finally break up?

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.620
Well, it was kind of a sea of blood.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.550
Is that true?

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.360
Well... it happened a long time ago.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.110
But why did he show up again?

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.780
Umm... Well... That's...

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.720
Listen to me, Yuusuke.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:33.230
Hotel Il Mare said they want to open a pastry shop under my name.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.130
Jean, that's great!

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.770
And that immediately brought your face to mind.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:43.540
The face of the only person in the world who can create the same tastes as me.

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.540
Your face...

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:52.170
You should come back to Paris and work for me again.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.760
I swear unconditionally...

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.310
I promise to pay you three times as much as you make now.

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:05.600
Three times as much...

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:11.320
If I was earning that much, I could buy a Hermes leather jacket, or a Goyard bag, without worrying.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:12.770
Sensei?

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.030
What?!

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.340
H-He's recruiting?

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.280
Yeah.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.540
Wh-What were the terms?

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:27.150
Working as a chef-pâtissier at his branch of the Hotel Il Mare in Paris.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:28.920
He said he'd pay me about 20 million yen per year.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.410
20 million?

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.300
Maybe it was 25 million.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:35.700
G-Gramps, you have to pay sensei more than that!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.040
I-I'm already paying more than any other shop.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.550
More than 25 million?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:41.600
No way.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:43.430
What should I do?

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.840
Sensei, don't...

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:48.700
If you leave this shop now, I...

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.380
I still have a lot to learn from you.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.320
Y-Yeah, you're right...

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.190
D-D-D-Does that mean Ono-san is leaving this shop?

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.420
That's no good, Ono-san!

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.430
Sensei!

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.650
Stop that.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.490
Outsiders shouldn't offer opinions.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.910
Yes...
Yeah...

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.320
In the end, Ono must decide for himself.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.320
Umm... hello, Mom?

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.930
How much free cash do I have now?

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.170
Eh? Not that much?

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.370
I see.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:27.770
No. If I borrow more, I won't be able to pay it back from my shop's annual take.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:37.780
Good afternoon.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:40.200
Welcome.

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:44.620
Our recommendation today is Compote Pêche avec Glacé Miel.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.950
Wh-What happened today?

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.280
You look very tired.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.880
Not at all.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:51.630
Please come in.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:53.060
Please take a seat.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.370
I don't mind doing take-out.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:01.050
Itou-san, I'm really glad that a kind person like you came today.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:06.030
Then I'll leave first.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:07.560
Ono.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.470
Are you in a hurry?

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.580
I have something to talk to you about.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.010
Umm... Okay.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:19.800
Umm...

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.880
W-W-W-Wait, Ono. Don't misunderstand me.

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:26.060
I would never, ever sleep with you.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.580
I won't sleep with you,

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.200
but if I said I would, would you stay at my shop?!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.090
How about another cup of coffee?

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.340
but if I said I would, would you stay at my shop?!

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.600
I wasn't even thinking of leaving your shop.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:56.880
And to be honest, I don't feel like sleeping with you now.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.290
You...

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:04.940
I said it like a virgin girl of the Edo period untying her robe in front of a villainous official, you bastard.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.280
S-Sorry, sorry.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:11.970
I've been worrying about how to refuse Jean.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:16.380
I don't know what he might do if he becomes enraged.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.920
You don't know what he might do...

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:22.480
I shouldn't have resumed a previous relationship, but I did.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:27.050
If I refuse, I have to be prepared for a bloodbath.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.490
Does he get pissed off easily?

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.380
Although he's not a bad person...

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.120
It's true.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.930
Come on. You're always joking.

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.150
How about another cup of coffee?

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:42.180
I assume you'll be in a dangerous situation sometime.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.400
Maybe.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:48.620
I never thought of taking care of myself.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:53.340
And I can't really control these things myself, can I?

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.960
Umm... Excuse me.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.110
Can I have a refill of coffee?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:57.320
Certainly.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:58.320
Can't control them...
Certainly.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.480
Can't control them...

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.500
Well, you really can't.

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.030
So... So...

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.800
You mean Ono-san will stay at our shop forever, right?

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.120
Yay! Yay!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:11.480
Well, I also really felt like cheering last night.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:14.980
Yay! Yay!
Well, I also really felt like cheering last night.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.120
Well, I also really felt like cheering last night.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:19.370
Eiji.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:20.670
Huh?

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.030
No, I haven't heard anything from Ono.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.950
That's strange.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.740
It's past the time he would normally show up at the shop.

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:31.390
But he's not picking up his home or cell phone.

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.200
Sensei has never been late before.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:36.800
Young master?

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.120
Did something happen to Ono-san?

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.950
Well, I don't know yet.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.340
Anyway, you go to the shop first.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.550
I'll go to Ono's place.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:48.720
I'm going with you!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:49.720
Come on.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.060
I <i>am</i> going with you.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.080
Ouch...

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.390
Ouch...

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:29.430
Gosh, I'm late!

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.930
So you're not going to think it over.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:33.680
Sorry...

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.090
Why?

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.570
Your pay would be three times higher.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:41.010
And isn't it easier for a gay like you to live in Paris than in Japan?

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:42.110
Sorry...

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.410
Why is it?

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.140
Yuusuke,

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:58.040
I could crush the fingers of your right hand now.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.210
Jean, y-you're joking, right?

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.420
Jean, y-you're joking, right?

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:21.520
Ono-san!

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.310
Geez, I thought it'd be like this.

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:33.340
Get away from Ono-san.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.590
Chikage-san, no!

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:41.060
Don't hurt his right hand!

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:43.150
He's got work to do after this.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:43.880
Let him go.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.290
He'll hurt you if I let him go!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.140
Let him go. Let him go, Chikage.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.840
He's saying he won't hurt Ono.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:03.830
Thank you.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.310
You came and saved me.

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.500
Geez.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:12.340
After something's happened, it's a bit late to think, "I don't want to die."

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:12.780
Sorry.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.700
I'll go to the shop first.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.890
You guys should come as soon as possible.

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.300
Are you all right?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.180
Yeah, I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:28.460
Something like this has happened several times before.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:32.380
Most times, I'm the one at fault.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.440
Please don't say s-such a sad thing.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:15.030
So Ono was injured in a quarrel with his ex-boyfriend, that blond guy who dropped in the other day.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:18.590
But when you see him, don't get pissed off and go running out for revenge!

00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:22.030
Hey, how could I fight a non-professional?

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.240
I'm a former pro-boxer.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:27.440
Sorry for being late.

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:29.030
Sensei...

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.850
That foreigner. How dare he do that to sensei.

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:35.130
Gramps!

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.280
Where did you say his hotel was?!

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:41.870
That's not what a former pro-boxer does, it's what a former gangster does.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:45.040
Jean is at the Hotel Il Mare.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:45.910
Would you like to come with me?

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:50.990
I'll pay, so have as many of his cakes as you want.

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:52.500
I'm sure you'll learn from them.

00:17:52.790 --> 00:17:56.340
And after you eat them, I don't think you'll want to hit him.

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:03.060
It really was like a French movie until the end.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.190
I'm sorry, Yuusuke.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.690
I was jealous of your talent all the time.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.440
I'm the one who has to apologize.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:19.600
To be honest,

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:25.350
I never thought that working as a pâtissier was fun.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:32.500
I only took the job because I had no other options.

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:37.710
But I now have an apprentice.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:41.440
He has good sense, and most of all, he likes making sweets.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.570
When I saw him, I thought,

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:47.930
"Ah! He could really become a great pâtissier"

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:57.400
So, I can't leave that shop until I teach him all my knowledge and skills.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:03.620
I want to make him a really great pâtissier, like you.

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:17.350
See you...

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.950
Oh! We have to make new cakes for winter.

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:30.010
Kanda-kun, you should make some trial pieces too.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:31.100
Are you sure?

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.310
Make them from start to finish, by myself?

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:33.740
Of course.

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:35.900
You're not an apprentice anymore.

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:40.550
Yes! I'll do my best!

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.140
Hey, hey, you guys! Especially Ono!

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:52.040
Payday!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.310
Yay.

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:56.380
Thanks, Tachibana.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.200
I love you.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.800
Idiot! Didn't I say it was just payday?

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:00.760
Hey, gramps.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:06.100
I don't want that money, so give it to sensei.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.740
Hey, Kanda-kun,

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.600
don't say something so generous.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.760
But I can't take it.

00:20:12.760 --> 00:20:14.010
Yeah.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:18.150
Even if you are an ex-world champion and don't need the money,

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.910
try to be a bit grateful.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.670
Eh? I don't have any money.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:27.190
I donated all the money I made from boxing to the orphanage where I grew up.

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:32.080
Wh-What a pure heart.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.920
Damn it. I thought I could get him to invest when I opened the second shop.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:43.140
But I was really frightened this morning, when I thought I was going to lose the use of my right hand.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:51.420
So I'll try to avoid getting involved in bloodbaths in the future.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:54.980
Maybe trying that now won't make a difference.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.390
I think it will make some difference.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:21:02.110
In fact, you're talking to women now, with a smile on your face.

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:08.730
That's what I'm talking about.

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:29.720
Now, let's open the shop!
